Build bookworm-uefi sdcard image for raspberrypi4b:

Input files ../kernel/linux/tmp/lib/modules/
            ../kernel/linux/tmp/boot/

cd ~/Downloads
wget https://mirror.us.mirhosting.net/debian-cd/12.11.0/arm64/iso-cd/debian-12.11.0-arm64-netinst.iso

cd ~/build-raspberrypi4b/bookworm-uefi

Plugin usb3 stick to PC.
sudo ./mksdcardimg.sh
sudo mkfs.vfat /dev/sda1
sudo fdisk -l /dev/sda
sudo mount /dev/sda1 /mnt
sudo 7z x ~/Downloads/debian-12.11.0-arm64-netinst.iso -o/mnt
sudo 7z x ~/Downloads/RPi4_UEFI_Firmware.zip -o/mnt
sync; sudo umount /mnt;
Eject usb3 stick from PC.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Install bookworm to usb3 stick.
NOTE: To minimize EMI interference, put usb3 stick to rpi4b top USB3 socket,
      Put keyboard mouse to rpi4b bottom USB2 socket with USB2 extention cable.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Plugin usb3 stick and ethernet cable to rpi4b. Power on rpi4b.
Esc -> Device Manager -> Rpi -> Advanced -> 3GB ( disable ) -> F10 -> Boot Manager -> first UEFI or SDCARD.
Select install
loading missing firmware? No
User name: linaro
Manual partion, select free, Automatic, All, Finish, Yes
Select debian desktop and gnome in addition to ssh and standard system utilities.

Plugin usb3 stick to PC.
sudo fdisk -l /dev/sda
sudo e2label /dev/sda2 rootfs
sudo blkid /dev/sda1 ( write down UUID )
sudo blkid /dev/sda2 ( write down UUID )
sudo mount /dev/sda2 /mnt
sudo cp -r ../kernel/linux/tmp/lib/modules/* /mnt/lib/modules
sudo cp -r ../kernel/linux/tmp/boot/* /mnt/boot
ls -la /mnt/boot
sudo touch /mnt/boot/grub/grub.cfg
sudo vi /mnt/boot/grub/grub.cfg ( delete everything, add
set timeout=5
set default="Boot UUID"
set menu_color_normal=white/black
set menu_color_highlight=white/green

menuentry "Boot UUID" {
    search --no-floppy --fs-uuid --set=root c9eba6c6-3c77-4f65-9647-269dff0145f8
    echo    'Loading Linux 6.18.0-v8+ ...'
    linux /boot/vmlinuz-6.18.0-v8+ root=LABEL=rootfs rootwait rw rootdelay=10
    echo    'Loading initial ramdisk ...'
    initrd /boot/initrd.img-6.1.0-41-arm64
    devicetree /boot/dtb/broadcom/bcm2711-rpi-4-b.dtb
}
)
sudo vi /mnt/etc/fstab ( change UUID for /boot/efi )
sudo cp ./packages/brcmfmac43455-sdio.txt /mnt/lib/firmware/brcm/
sudo cp ./packages/BCM4345C0.hcd /mnt/lib/firmware/brcm/
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/lib/firmware/rtl_bt
sudo cp ./packages/rtl* /mnt/lib/firmware/rtl_bt
ls -la /mnt/lib/firmware/rtl_bt
sync; sudo umount /mnt;
Eject usb3 stick from PC. 

Plugin usb3 stick to rpi4b, Unplug ethernet cable from rpi4b. Power on rpi4b.
Setup wifi. Disable power saving, auto suspend and screen saver.
su -
usermod -aG adm,sudo,video linaro
sync
reboot

sudo apt install openssh-server net-tools pulseaudio-utils
sudo ifconfig
uname -a
lsb_release -a
sudo apt update; sudo apt upgrade;
sync
free

Install mesa 25:
su -
export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
echo "deb http://deb.debian.org/debian bookworm-backports main" > /etc/apt/sources.list.d/backports.list
apt update
apt install -t bookworm-backports -y --no-install-recommends mesa-vulkan-drivers mesa-va-drivers libgl1-mesa-dri libglx-mesa0 libegl-mesa0 libgbm1 libgles2-mesa
ldconfig
exit
sync
free
sudo update-initramfs -u -k $(uname -r)
sudo vi /boot/grub/grub.cfg ( change to:
   initrd /boot/initrd.img-6.18.0-v8+
)
sync
sudo reboot

uname -a
lsb_release -a
sudo cat /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq/scaling_cur_freq
Check if Debian is running UEFI mode:
ls /sys/firmware/efi
Check display mode: ( wayland or x11 )
echo $XDG_SESSION_TYPE
Check audio driver: ( pulseaudio or pipewire )
pactl info

sudo apt install git zip rfkill speedtest-cli python3-pip python3-setuptools ffmpeg mpv glmark2-es2-wayland vlc vlc-plugin-video-output firefox-esr vsftpd pavucontrol

speedtest-cli --secure

glmark2-es2-wayland

aplay -l
pavucontrol  ( select hdmi as default )

firefox -> youtube.com -> search YmDNhi07_Ho

Do follows on PC, then ftp swan.mp4 to rpi4b.
(
git clone https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp.git
cd yt-dlp
make
cd ../
~/yt-dlp/yt-dlp -f 'bestvideo[ext=mp4][protocol=https]+bestaudio[ext=m4a][protocol=https]' 3qrKjywjo7Q -o swan.mp4 --postprocessor-args " -c:v libx264 -b:v 2M -c:a copy"
)

mpv swan.mp4
ffplay swan.mp4
cvlc --gl=wgl --glconv=any swan.mp4

Plugin ASUS USB-BT500 bluetooth usb dongle to rpi4b.
sudo rfkill list
hciconfig hci0
hcitool dev
hciconfig -a
